        <item>
            <key> <string>description</string> </key>
            <value> <string encoding="cdata"><![CDATA[

Create or patch a portal callable (Python Script or MCP Tool in portal_callables) WITHOUT sending the whole source. Pass `replacements` (a list of {old_string, new_string, replace_all}) to apply Claude-Code-style exact edits to the callable\'s body - each old_string must match exactly once unless replace_all=true - or `body`/`text_content` for the full source. `params` sets the callable\'s parameter signature directly (Zope _params). For an MCP Tool, `input_schema`/`output_schema` are written into the sibling <id>_spec JSON Form (text_content / response_schema) and the tool\'s Python signature is re-derived from that spec via setParameterSignatureFromSpecification (what mcp_tool_workflow does on a spec change). Creates the callable when missing (portal_type \'Python Script\' or \'MCP Tool\'). DEV/DESTRUCTIVE: deploys server-side callable code.

]]></string> </value>
